    {
      "id": "rule.meme-pipeline-routing",
      "type": "routing-rule",
      "name": "Meme pipeline and provider routing",
      "aliases": [
        "which model for a meme",
        "meme provider",
        "v2v provider",
        "meme edit model",
        "meme routing"
      ],
      "source": "knowledge/memes/muha-meds.json",
      "rules": [
        "Video meme that must keep the original footage => MiniMax H3 v2v (pipeline B); the only provider that edits actor footage. Seedance 2.0/2.5, NB Pro, FLUX 3 Video, Kling Motion Control refuse or fail.",
        "Video meme that can be re-staged with devices as characters => NB Pro start frame from a BLOCKING DIAGRAM (never the film frame) + Veo 3.1 i2v (pipeline A).",
        "Still meme => gpt-image-2 /v1/images/edits with the frame as REFERENCE 1 and the device Front+45 renders as refs (pipeline C); Nano Banana Pro when gpt refuses (classical nudes) or hands must be repainted to grip (pipeline D); Seedream v5 Pro is_inpaint for per-panel stills with real actors (pipeline E).",
        "Never composite/PIL-paste a device or badge into a meme; generate with the real asset as a reference.",
        "Captions, labels, watermarks: composed deterministically after generation (card.py / memecard.sh / buildcard.py). Never model-drawn.",
        "Run a control before concluding a provider refuses the material; gpt-image-2 rejects ~1 in 4 candidates at random — over-request.",
        "Always show a real SKU from the device's pair table; never invent a pairing."
      ],
      "categories": [
        "memes"
      ]
    },
